  "details": "Since VRC recently provided a couple camera updates this week, I've wanted to mention one change that I've been hoping will eventually come with it. Basically, just a toggle to allow the camera UI (while in VR) to track your head instead of your local position.\n\nTo clarify, I'm NOT referring to what the lens is recording/pointing at; I'm referring to where the actual camera tablet is floating. Let it follow where your head rotates to.\n\nThere's already head tracking available for Personal Mirrors, but mirrors disappear through walls and floors. I just want to be able to keep myself in view while doing yoga and not have to grab and re-adjust the camera UI every few seconds :,3 It would also be very good for anyone who spins and turns around a lot in VR, and uses the camera to keep spatial awareness/visual on their tracking. Not having to grab the camera and put it back in front of me every few seconds would be very nice.\n\nThanks for reading!",
